1
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:42,490
[She's Wild Fire]

2
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:47,640
[Episode 23: Wherever You Go, I Go]

3
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:54,340
Morning.

4
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:55,400
Morning.

5
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:58,160
Where's Biao and the others?

6
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:59,600
He went to check the cargo.

7
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,130
Waiting for the last batch.

8
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,670
Didn't you have a meeting
with the Harboria client this morning?

9
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:08,600
Why are you here?

10
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:10,720
The client rescheduled.

11
00:01:12,039 --> 00:01:13,240
I brought breakfast.

12
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:14,200
We've got...

13
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,600
Shumai, shrimp dumplings,

14
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:16,520
and sushi.

15
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:18,250
And hot soy milk.

16
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:19,330
What do you want?

17
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:44,140
I saw nothing. I saw nothing.

18
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,930
You're asking for trouble!

19
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:50,800
Ms. Xie, Mr. Chu, please carry on.

20
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,200
I'm invisible.

21
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,039
Biao,

22
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,680
you finished checking the cargo?

23
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:56,520
Ms. Xie,

24
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:57,600
all done.

25
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,320
Everything is set up just as you ordered.

26
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:00,250
Good work, Biao.

27
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:02,480
Ms. Xie,

28
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,880
two more overseas orders just came in.

29
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,440
One from a boutique in Milan,

30
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:08,440
and another
from a department store in London.

31
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,400
Milan?

32
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:10,800
London?

33
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:13,640
We've expanded our business
right into the heart of Europe.

34
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:14,440
Mr. Chu,

35
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:17,200
once the funds from this batch come in,

36
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:19,520
plus these new orders,

37
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,300
shouldn't we have a proper celebration?

38
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,920
As for me,

39
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,170
I just do whatever Ms. Xie says.

40
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:27,880
Alright.

41
00:02:28,079 --> 00:02:29,520
Then I'll give the order.

42
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,600
Once these goods are delivered,

43
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:33,240
and our funds are secured,

44
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,040
I suggest

45
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:37,240
we all go to Europe together!

46
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,880
Awesome!

47
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,520
We'll go to Paris, to Milan.

48
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,720
And watch Formula 1 racing!

49
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,120
Ms. Xie,

50
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,700
can I go

51
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,240
see the Mona Lisa?

52
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:53,920
Of course.

53
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,560
And, um...

54
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:58,480
A boat ride on the Seine,

55
00:02:58,640 --> 00:02:59,880
the Champs-Élysées,

56
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:02,200
and Left Bank coffee.

57
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,920
And Milan Cathedral,

58
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,320
and Lake Como.

59
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:06,640
And while we're at it,

60
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:10,320
we can also check out
their fabric production.

61
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,440
Ms. Xie,

62
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:17,480
are we going out to play,

63
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:18,680
or to work?

64
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,400
It's a win-win.

65
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,290
Let's go. It's time.

66
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,120
Load the cargo onto the ship.

67
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,130
Let's go!

68
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:42,400
Ms. Wan,

69
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,800
we're far enough from the port.

70
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:45,760
Hurry up!

71
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,620
Where's the cargo?

72
00:04:05,070 --> 00:04:06,030
Where is it?

73
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,840
Where are my goods?

74
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:09,440
Where are my goods?!

75
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,400
Ms. Wan,

76
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,600
since when

77
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,360
did my qipaos become your goods?

78
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,079
Xie Nanfeng?

79
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,920
We've been tailing you all the way.

80
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,040
You finally

81
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:24,720
slipped up.

82
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:26,920
So,

83
00:04:27,250 --> 00:04:29,050
are you satisfied with my goods?

84
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:30,960
I carefully

85
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,940
picked them out for you from the junkyard.

86
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:35,340
They should perfectly match your current

87
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,880
vibe and situation.

88
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,520
Xie Nanfeng!

89
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,520
You set me up!

90
00:04:46,159 --> 00:04:47,000
Set you up?

91
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,520
You were the one plotting
where you shouldn't have.

92
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:52,920
Using an affiliated logistics company
to steal

93
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,450
and swap clients' goods...

94
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:57,280
that's not business competition anymore.

95
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,120
It's a crime.

96
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:01,800
You guessed right.

97
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,080
On Xunda Logistics' shareholder list,

98
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,410
Ms. Wan is indeed there.

99
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,240
She just holds a very small stake,

100
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,500
and used her real name,

101
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,100
which is why she flew under the radar.

102
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,080
Then it's not hard to explain

103
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,040
why on this ship,

104
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,970
we couldn't find
any outbound declaration records.

105
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,440
As far as I know,

106
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,040
Mr. Chen from Xunda

107
00:05:26,070 --> 00:05:28,000
has always valued his reputation.

108
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:29,560
Right, Ms. Wan?

109
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:34,810
I wonder how he punishes traitors.

110
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:35,360
You!

111
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,360
Now it's truly resolved.

112
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:01,160
As long as we have our own shipping line,

113
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,300
we can truly go global.

114
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,760
Then I have some good news for you.

115
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:08,680
I bought

116
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:11,680
two mid-sized freighters
from Yongchang Shipping.

117
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,320
It also comes with their

118
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:15,000
small berths in Shekou,

119
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,330
and a five-year lease on their warehouse.

120
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,480
You...

121
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,520
bought a shipping route?

122
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:26,500
More accurately, we've temporarily secured

123
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:30,040
an entire shipping route
under our own control.

124
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:33,600
The ships are a bit old,

125
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,240
but well-maintained.

126
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,600
And they perfectly fit

127
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:38,530
our cargo volume and voyage needs.

128
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,400
Even though the initial investment

129
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,520
took up most of our cash flow,

130
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,880
but

131
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:46,520
in the long run,

132
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,880
having the lifeline of logistics

133
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,800
in our own hands

134
00:06:50,710 --> 00:06:51,840
is totally worth it.

135
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,840
Oh, Ms. Xie,

136
00:06:57,490 --> 00:06:59,690
how do you always manage to surprise me?

137
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,810
You can handle everything so well,

138
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,920
and so thoroughly.

139
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,800
You leave me no chance to step in.

140
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,680
Looks like

141
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:13,640
I should cause my Mr. Chu

142
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,120
a bit more trouble,

143
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,800
so he won't know what to do with me.

144
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:19,320
Right?

145
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:22,430
Cheers.

146
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,720
Ms. Xie,

147
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:37,140
you should take a break too.

148
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:38,680
If anything comes up,

149
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,600
just leave it to me.

150
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:45,200
I can't.

151
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:48,000
I still have to rush to customs.

152
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:49,880
You can't rest either.

153
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:52,400
Hurry up and
review all the reports for me.

154
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,000
Madam Hong,

155
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:56,640
why are you here?

156
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:58,000
I didn't come to see you.

157
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,400
I just went to your place to see Nannan.

158
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,040
I was missing my daughter-in-law!

159
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:03,640
Feng,

160
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,720
I made some soup for you.

161
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:05,480
Have a taste.

162
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
None for you!

163
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,040
None for you.

164
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:13,960
Then I won't hold back.

165
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,290
I simmered it for hours.

166
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:17,280
This chicken soup

167
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:19,880
isn't something just anyone gets to drink.

168
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,000
Is it good?

169
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:26,380
Delicious.

170
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:40,200
Alright.

171
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,400
I got it.

172
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:44,200
Madam Hong,

173
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,800
I'm really sorry,

174
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,400
but I have to rush to customs.

175
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,200
How about this,

176
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,720
next time I'm free,

177
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,050
I'll take you shopping.

178
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,440
Okay, go ahead.

179
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:01,680
Drink slowly.

180
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,680
Madam Hong's chicken soup,

181
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:06,520
wish me luck!

182
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:11,410
She's so full of fire,

183
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,040
just like me when I was young.

184
00:09:15,590 --> 00:09:16,930
Not like when you offered a hundred grand

185
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:18,130
to sell off your son?

186
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,400
Why bring that up!

187
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,200
Mom,

188
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:24,730
is there really none for me?

189
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:25,800
When Feng gets back,

190
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,660
make sure she drinks all the soup!

191
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:31,600
Okay, got it.
